§ `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene helpers: three-valued logic`

-- Strong Kleene logic, written from the truth tables, not from the code. They carry the FALSE and NOTHING of their arguments and add no reading of the Act.
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
